# TASK A1 – DECOMPOSE THE PROGRAM INTO FUNCTIONS

## A1.1 – Identify the Functions (2 Marks)

The District Blood Bank Network program is divided into smaller functions. Each function performs one specific operation. This makes the program modular, easier to test and maintain.

### Functions and their responsibilities

| Function | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `registerDonor()` | Registers a new donor. |
| `checkEligibility()` | Checks whether a donor is eligible to donate. |
| `findDonors()` | Finds donors belonging to a particular blood group. |
| `updateStock()` | Updates available blood units after donation or issue. |
| `findYoungestEligible()` | Finds the number of eligible donors and youngest donor. |
| `saveDonors()` | Saves donor records into a file. |
| `loadDonors()` | Loads donor records from a file. |
| `saveStock()` | Saves stock records into a file. |
| `loadStock()` | Loads stock records from a file. |
| `displayReport()` | Displays donor and stock information. |

### Structure Chart

```text
                 MAIN PROGRAM
                       |
       +---------------+----------------+
       |               |                |
  Load Records    Process Operations   Save Records
       |               |                |
   +---+---+       +---+---+        +---+---+
   |       |       |       |        |       |
Load    Load   Register Find    Save    Save
Donors  Stock  Donor   Donors  Donors  Stock
                   |       |
               Check    Display
             Eligibility Report
                   |
              Update Stock
```

The main program controls the overall execution. It calls the required functions to load records, process donor operations, update stock and save the results.

## A1.2 – Design the Interfaces (3 Marks)

### Function Prototypes

```c
typedef struct {
    int id;
    char name[50];
    char bloodGroup[4];
    int age;
    char phone[15];
    char lastDonation[11];
} Donor;

typedef struct {
    char bloodGroup[4];
    int units;
} Stock;

